{"availability":"available","full":"thanhng8/supertonic-tool","name":"supertonic-tool","description":"tools that help during the use of supertonic","category":"Developer tools","language":"Swift","stars":90,"forks":46,"created":"2026-05-13T11:06:38Z","updated":"2026-05-18T01:27:18Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Supertone/supertonic-3","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:22.696Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:22.696Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:22.696Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:00:22.696Z","stars":90,"forks":46}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A small toolkit I built on top of Supertone's Supertonic to turn the TTS engine into a local WebSocket server with a feature-rich browser client. Everything in this section lives in tool/ and is not part of the upstream project.","Supertonic by Supertone Inc. is a lightning-fast, on-device TTS system powered by ONNX Runtime. It runs fully offline, supports 31 languages, and ships with ready-to-use examples in Python, Node.js, Browser, Java, C++, C#, Go, Swift, Rust, iOS, and Flutter (see the corresponding folders in this repo)."],"features":["🚀 One-click / one-command launchers — Windows .bat plus Ubuntu/macOS .sh, both auto-install deps and boot the server.","⚡ Accelerated when available — auto-detects CUDA → DirectML → CoreML → CPU with CPU fallback if an accelerator fails.","🧠 Batch inference — multiple requests within a 100 ms window are merged into a single GPU call, so 6 lines render as fast as 1.","🎭 Multi-line dialogue queue — assign a different voice/language per line for true conversational TTS.","📥 Bulk import — load dialogue from .xlsx, .csv, .txt, or markdown tables."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/thanhng8/supertonic-tool/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"778870a53965df017356e4c50a69a65e7fc1a6f4f2c1b31433f3b0c990c8d9a1","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:0